public with sharing class AccountCountrySync {

    /**
     * When an Account's BillingCountry changes, sets MailingCountry to the new
     * BillingCountry on that Account's Contacts whose MailingCountry is blank or
     * equal to the Account's previous BillingCountry. All other Contacts are untouched.
     */
    public static void syncContactCountries(List<Account> newAccounts, Map<Id, Account> oldMap) {
        if (newAccounts == null || newAccounts.isEmpty() || oldMap == null) {
            return;
        }

        // accountId -> previous BillingCountry, accountId -> new BillingCountry
        Map<Id, String> previousCountryByAccountId = new Map<Id, String>();
        Map<Id, String> newCountryByAccountId = new Map<Id, String>();

        for (Account acc : newAccounts) {
            Account oldAcc = oldMap.get(acc.Id);
            if (oldAcc == null) {
                continue;
            }
            if (acc.BillingCountry != oldAcc.BillingCountry) {
                previousCountryByAccountId.put(acc.Id, oldAcc.BillingCountry);
                newCountryByAccountId.put(acc.Id, acc.BillingCountry);
            }
        }

        // No billing country changes in this batch: no query, no DML.
        if (newCountryByAccountId.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Single query, scoped to only the changed accounts' contacts.
        List<Contact> toUpdate = new List<Contact>();
        for (Contact con : [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :newCountryByAccountId.keySet()
        ]) {
            String previousCountry = previousCountryByAccountId.get(con.AccountId);
            if (String.isBlank(con.MailingCountry) || con.MailingCountry == previousCountry) {
                con.MailingCountry = newCountryByAccountId.get(con.AccountId);
                toUpdate.add(con);
            }
        }

        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

**What I changed and why**

- **I did not use `[SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry FROM Contact]` with no filter.** With about 2.3 million contacts, that query would exceed the 50,000-row SOQL governor limit and fail on every batch. It would also load millions of records into heap memory. Instead, the query filters with `WHERE AccountId IN :changedAccountIds`, which returns only contacts of accounts whose BillingCountry actually changed. It still runs once per trigger invocation, not once per account or per contact, so the bulk-safety goal holds.
- **The query runs only when there is a change.** If no account in the batch changed its BillingCountry, the handler returns before querying.
- **Contacts are filtered in memory.** The previous country differs per account, so the in-memory check (`blank` or equal to that account's previous country) is simpler than building a dynamic SOQL filter. Only contacts of changed accounts are in the result set, so this is cheap.
- **One update DML at the end.** Contacts are collected and updated in a single statement, and that statement is skipped when nothing qualifies.
- **Sharing.** The class uses `with sharing`, so the running user's record access applies. If the MDM integration user cannot see all contacts, some will be skipped silently. If you need a complete sync regardless of user visibility, switch to `without sharing` after reviewing the security implications.

**Things to check in the org**

- If Country/State picklists are enabled, `MailingCountry` and `BillingCountry` are picklists. Values must be valid for the target field or the update will fail.
- If BillingCountry is cleared on an account, this code blanks the MailingCountry of matching contacts. That follows the stated rule, but you may prefer to skip the sync when the new value is blank.

