The component had five problems: it mutated `heading` in place, so later parent changes were ignored; it aliased the parent's `tasks` array and objects; it pushed into arrays without reassigning, so the UI didn't re-render; it dispatched `taskAdded` where the spec requires `taskadded`; and its toggle handler didn't reliably match ids. The fix below copies the parent's tasks, uses immutable updates, derives the upper-case heading in a getter, and dispatches `taskadded` with the trimmed label. The markup keeps the same elements, classes and `data-id`s; only the heading binding changes to the new getter.

